From ea42d1068ea0be0fe9f3fc278a4a2560b796a65d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JingMatrix <jingmatrix@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 13:32:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/47] Package the module for every 64-bit ABI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Build the interceptor for each 64-bit ABI — keystore2 is 64-bit on every supported
device — and lay the binaries out per ABI; service.sh injects the set matching the
running device. package.sh builds the ABIs and zips them, needing only the NDK.

At boot service.sh injects into keystore2 and re-injects on every restart. keystore2
is unprivileged, so it also opens traversal of /data/adb and makes the keybox
world-readable; the keybox stays a user-supplied file and is never shipped. The
injector passes keystore2 the library as a file descriptor over a unix socket, which
its SELinux domain cannot do by default, so sepolicy.rule grants just those accesses
between the keystore and injector domains, keeping keystore enforcing.
